WEBVTT

00:00:00.865 --> 00:00:03.600
You know that moment when everything works...

00:00:03.667 --> 00:00:04.720
until you reboot?

00:00:05.640 --> 00:00:07.260
The service is running.

00:00:07.300 --> 00:00:08.780
The port is open.

00:00:08.860 --> 00:00:10.940
Then suddenly, you can't reach it.

00:00:11.954 --> 00:00:14.380
That's the kind of mistake Autorelabel helps you catch.

00:00:15.393 --> 00:00:20.700
It gives you timed RHCSA and RHCE practice exams on real RHEL 10

00:00:20.740 --> 00:00:23.260
virtual machines, right on your Linux computer.

00:00:23.409 --> 00:00:25.180
Twenty tasks.

00:00:25.220 --> 00:00:26.300
Three hundred points.

00:00:26.540 --> 00:00:28.460
A lab you can actually work in.

00:00:30.125 --> 00:00:34.060
And when you submit, every exam node reboots before your work is scored.

00:00:36.020 --> 00:00:37.620
The service still starts.

00:00:37.720 --> 00:00:40.100
The SELinux label is still there.

00:00:40.180 --> 00:00:42.900
But that firewall rule you only changed at runtime?

00:00:43.092 --> 00:00:43.940
Gone.

00:00:46.025 --> 00:00:49.640
You see which checks passed, what didn't survive, and how to fix it.

00:00:49.800 --> 00:00:51.480
Review the solution.

00:00:51.580 --> 00:00:52.840
Try the exam again.

00:00:53.020 --> 00:00:55.560
And get comfortable making changes that last.

00:00:55.864 --> 00:00:57.320
Autorelabel.

00:00:57.464 --> 00:00:58.760
Make it survive.
